.TH freshcrab 1  "freshcrab 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
freshcrab \- Automatic updater and validator for openSUSE Tumbleweed/Factory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfreshcrab\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-packages\fR] [\fB\-\-queue\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-live\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report\-only by default: prints the queue (packages behind on Factory) and files nothing. Dry\-run mode (default true) is global: the watcher polls the collectors and prints what it WOULD queue, the queue evaluates the dedup rules and prints the decision for each candidate, and the dispatcher logs the would\-do plan and the exact SR payload and files nothing. All plan output goes to stderr, so stdout stays machine\-readable JSON. Report\-only mode gates only the dispatcher: the watcher still runs and produces its entries; in live mode it enqueues and the queue state file is still written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<path>\fR [default: config.yaml]
path to config.yaml
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI<pkg>...\fR
check only these packages (overrides the config list). Repeated use accumulates
.TP
\fB\-\-queue\fR \fI<path>\fR [default: queue.json]
path to the queue state file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
force dry\-run mode (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-live\fR
force live mode (writes the queue; overrides config and env)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
